{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T00:44:50.340Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-1","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"fe411f5ac7c0c68c436d07f8","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-1","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1627","claim:pm-gh1628","lineage:pm-gh1627","lineage:pm-5t33or","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1627+pm-gh1628","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1627","claim:pm-gh1628","lineage:pm-gh1627","lineage:pm-5t33or","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T00:44:50.340Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Independent measurement on current source (229 open items, 112 ready) before the fix: pm next --limit 5 TOON 9,148 bytes / 83 lines, 182 escaped-quote sequences, 30 null cells, 4 *_encoding blocks; filters.token_budget reported 640 while nothing enforced it and no read_output receipt was emitted. --token-budget 640 trimmed only recommended+ready (ready_budget estimated 628 within_budget true) and the response stayed 8,879 bytes: the legacy cost alias replaced the universal default ceiling (4000 TOON / 6000 JSON) and resolveBindingReadOutputBudget ignores legacy cost outside context, so the whole-response ceiling was removed rather than applied. The canonical --output-budget 640 omitted the entire result (requested_budget_infeasible; floor of one row per collection + envelope = 1,251 tokens). Codec probe: the compact table candidate lost for ready (1,634 vs 1,592 bytes) and containers (1,805 vs 1,767) only because omitting one all-null column emitted a 15-name column_order list, so those sections fell back to escaped tag JSON; decision_needed and blocked already used list columns."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T00:44:50.340Z"}],"before_hash":"5c487c03d8c2f8a6ee3ad244814f6b3ece672d8425cc05341c0c6de5a9c1fa0d","after_hash":"76c735caf89e0a10d944c99cfee49649f3ff80d1ab43a4f771cc96c59d70d902","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"94b95c0b3ce6919d5e9b73cb40f79410c0a341b150a032fed94aae092c85a949"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T00:44:50.845Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-1","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"fe411f5ac7c0c68c436d07f8","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-1","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1627","claim:pm-gh1628","lineage:pm-gh1627","lineage:pm-5t33or","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1627+pm-gh1628","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1627","claim:pm-gh1628","lineage:pm-gh1627","lineage:pm-5t33or","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T00:44:50.845Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Fix: (1) PmTableCellEncoding emits null_column_index (original position per omitted null column) instead of the full column_order list; decoders still accept legacy column_order. (2) --token-budget is no longer a read-output cost alias for next, so the universal default ceiling keeps binding the complete response. (3) A requested selection budget always audits the complete envelope: read_output now reports budget_source default, budget_tokens and estimated_tokens beside truncation.ready_budget; an enforced --for intent receipt suppresses the duplicate audit. (4) filters.token_budget is the requested selection ceiling or null. After the fix on the same tracker: TOON default 8,718 bytes (-430), escaped quotes 76 (-106; the remainder is the blockers object column on blocked/containers rows), null cells 15, every section list-encodes tags; pm next --limit 5 --token-budget 640 --json carries read_output {budget_source: default, budget_tokens: 6000, estimated_tokens: 4119, within_budget: true} and filters.token_budget 640; the default run reports token_budget null and no receipt. Gates: token-budget gate (32 surfaces) and context-intent calibration pass; SDK surface snapshot updated with an acknowledgement for NextResult.filters.token_budget (number|null) and the new codec field. Negative control: with the four source files stashed the three new tests fail (expected 640 to be null; null_column_index undefined; legacy order b,a,c)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T00:44:50.845Z"}],"before_hash":"76c735caf89e0a10d944c99cfee49649f3ff80d1ab43a4f771cc96c59d70d902","after_hash":"fd279ac89cb34b4b8c70814d063e7eeedef925dc61d5f6df3e1f794122e84c70","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"74657c0ab3b7a12db036d49a80568d4f5e40e9113773bc410afa3d9029fbccff"}
